cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Rigidity of harmonic functions on the supercritical percolation cluster: Lean formalization"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Percolation-Rigidity"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Rigidity of harmonic functions on the
  supercritical percolation cluster" by Ahmed Bou-Rabee, William Cooperman and Paul Dario, in a
  corrected draft of the arXiv v2 source kept in paper/. All 43 numbered results that the paper
  proves are proved in Lean, with no sorry and only the standard axioms, from twelve results of the
  literature that enter as explicit hypotheses; the other five numbered results are quoted from the
  literature. Among them are the main theorems: on the infinite cluster of supercritical bond
  percolation, Lipschitz harmonic functions and integer-valued harmonic functions of linear growth
  are constant (Theorems 1.1 and 1.2), in two dimensions a function with integer Laplacian of finite
  support that decays faster than |x|^-1 has finite support (Theorem 1.3), and the sandpile Markov
  chain on the largest cluster of a box mixes in time of order n^d log n (Theorem 6.5). Each of the
  four main theorems has a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - percolation
  - harmonic functions
  - stochastic homogenization
  - abelian sandpile
